       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day. That is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day (often limited to 3,000 mg/day in hospitalized patients). A single 3,000 mg dose is also well above the normal 500\u20131,000 mg per dose. This amount could cause serious liver toxicity, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **1,000 mg by mouth three times daily** (3,000 mg/day total)\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours** (about 2,600 mg/day)\n- **3,000 mg/day total**, split into smaller doses\n\nTell me which you want, or give me a different regimen, and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm the dose with your supervising resident or pharmacist if you're unsure."
